🟠 **High** `provider/codexUsageLimits.ts:266`

When a notification updates an exhausted window without `resetsAt` while the first quota read is pending, reconciliation drops the read's reset timestamp, so `codexUsageLimitResetAt` returns `null` and the terminal never auto-recovers. `laterReport` falls back to `notified` when its reset is absent; preserve `read.resetsAt` while keeping the notification's usage.

```diff
-  return notified &&
-    read &&
-    notified.resetsAt != null &&
-    notified.resetsAt === read.resetsAt &&
-    used(read) > used(notified)
-    ? read
-    : notified;
+  if (!notified || !read) return notified;
+  if (notified.resetsAt == null && read.resetsAt != null) {
+    return { ...notified, resetsAt: read.resetsAt };
+  }
+  return notified.resetsAt != null &&
+    notified.resetsAt === read.resetsAt &&
+    used(read) > used(notified)
+    ? read
+    : notified;
```

